    {
      "type": "tweet",
      "id": "2006572663339131196",
      "url": "https://x.com/Ammar1176708/status/2006572663339131196",
      "twitterUrl": "https://twitter.com/Ammar1176708/status/2006572663339131196",
      "text": "🌍 LIVE EARTH MONITORING REPORT\n🛰️ https://t.co/O8uWWmbiJj — Real-time seismic & volcanic watch\nToday’s earthquakes are clustering along the Pacific Ring of Fire, directly linked to major volcanic systems. Below is a location-by-location correlation ⬇️\n\n🔥 BANDA SEA — M5.4 EARTHQUAKE\n📍 Deep tectonic zone, Indonesia\n\nNearest volcanoes:\n• 🌋 Banda Api — active volcanic island\n• 🌋 Mount Nila — historical eruptions\n• 🌋 Mount Wurlali (Damar Island) — active stratovolcano\n🧠 Cause: Subduction of the Indo-Australian Plate beneath the Banda Arc\n⚠️ Note: Earthquakes here often precede volcanic unrest\n\n🔥 PHILIPPINES — M5.0 EARTHQUAKE (SE of Pondaguitan)\nNearest active volcanoes:\n• 🌋 Mount Kanlaon — erupted in 2025\n• 🌋 Mount Mayon — one of the world’s most active\n• 🌋 Mount Bulusan — frequent ash emissions\n• 🌋 Mount Pinatubo — historically explosive\n🧠 Cause: Complex collision of Philippine Sea Plate & Eurasian Plate\n⚠️ High volcano density zone\n🌋 CALIFORNIA, USA — Multiple Small Quakes\n\nNearest volcanic systems:\n• 🌋 The Geysers Geothermal Field\n• 🌋 Clear Lake Volcanic Field\n• 🌋 Long Valley Caldera (regional influence)\n🧠 Cause: San Andreas Fault system\nℹ️ Mostly tectonic, but geothermal activity present\n\n❄️ ALASKA — M2.2 (SW of Susitna)\n\nNearest volcanoes:\n• 🌋 Mount Spurr\n• 🌋 Mount Redoubt\n• 🌋 Mount Iliamna\n🧠 Cause: Pacific Plate subducting under North American Plate\n⚠️ One of Earth’s most active volcano-earthquake regions\n🌊 PUERTO RICO — M2.5 (Las Marías)\nNearest volcanic feature:\n• 🌋 Puerto Rico Trench (submarine system)\n🧠 Cause: Caribbean–North American Plate boundary\nℹ️ Mostly tectonic, limited surface volcanism\n\n📡 SPACE TRACKER INSIGHT\nEarthquakes and volcanoes are not random — they are surface signals of deep planetary mechanics.\nWhere plates collide, magma rises.\nWe are monitoring these zones live.\n\n🛰️ Follow for real-time Earth & space intelligence\n🔭 https://t.co/O8uWWmbiJj\n\n🔥 #Earthquake\n#Volcano\n#RingOfFire\n#Seismology\n#Volcanology\n#BreakingNews\n#EarthScience\n#Geology\n#NaturalDisasters\n#SpaceTracker\n#LiveMonitoring\n#BandaSea\n#Philippines\n#Indonesia\n#Alaska\n#California",
